      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T16:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t be used with `const`. `cstr!` uses `unwrap()` and it\u0027s prohibited for `const` variables. Here\u0027s relevant compilation error.\n\n```\nerror[E0015]: cannot call non-const fn `Result::\u003c\u0026CStr, FromBytesWithNulError\u003e::unwrap` in constants\n```\n\nI also tried `lazy_static!` but it didn\u0027t support `nostd` in its `Android.bp`.\n\n\nI personally prefer this, but I can change this with const byte literals and calls `cstr!()` whenever it\u0027s necessary. What do you think? Feel free to comment here if you prefer other way.",
      "parentUuid": "97d9077a_df2d981e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "62ae466729963fb073b1f2b484c1d8fe96679117",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
